L753: 6
L754: 3: Biomarker analytical methodology
L755: Following collection, EDTA plasma samples were pre-treated with the alkylating agent N-ethylmaleimide to
L756: prevent artefactual oxidation,(10) immediately centrifuged, then snap frozen in liquid nitrogen before storage at
L757: -80 [o] C until analysis. Serum samples were allowed to stand for 30 minutes at room temperature before
L758: centrifugation, snap freezing and storage at -80 [o] C.
L759: **Thiol redox metabolome**
L760: Total free thiols, which mostly reflect the availability of a single free cysteine group (Cys-34) of albumin, were
L761: measured as a marker of whole-body redox status (with higher values representing increased antioxidant
L762: capacity and/or enhanced propensity for disulfide reduction) and were determined spectrophotometrically using
L763: Ellman's reagent (5,5'-dithio-bis-2-nitrobenzoic acid; DTNB) and normalised to protein concentration.(11)
L764: Free aminothiols and hydrogen sulfide (H2S), which included the reduced and oxidised forms of glutathione
L765: (reduced glutathione [free GSH] and glutathione disulfide [GSSG]), cysteine (reduced cysteine [free Cys] and
L766: cystine [CySS]), homocysteine (reduced homocysteine [free HCys] and homocystine [HCySS]), and free and
L767: oxidised sulfide, were quantified from EDTA plasma pretreated with N-ethylmaleimide (NEM) using ultrahigh
L768: pressure liquid chromatography-electrospray ionization-tandem mass spectrometry (UPLC-ESI-MS/MS); free and
L769: bound thiols were quantified before and after reduction of plasma aliquots by dithiothreitol as previously
L770: described(12). Redox couples were calculated e.g., free GSH/GSSG, free CyS/CySS, free HCyS/HCySS as markers
L771: of extracellular redox potential.
L772: **Lipid peroxidation**
L773: Whole-body lipid peroxidation status was measured as thiobarbituric acid reactive substances (TBARS) in serum
L774: by the malondialdehyde (MDA) colorimetric assay.(13, 14) 4-Hydroxynonenal (4-HNE) concentrations were
L775: quantified as a downstream marker of lipid peroxidation from EDTA plasma samples using the enzyme-linked
L776: immunosorbent assay (ELISA) technique (4-HNE micro-ELISA plate - Elabscience® USA [Detection range 0.63 - 40
L777: ng/ml]).
L778: **FRAP assay**
L779: The ferric reducing ability of plasma (FRAP) was quantified as a measure of total antioxidant capacity. The FRAP
L780: assay measures the reduction of ferric (Fe [3+] ) to ferrous (Fe [2+] ) ions by the formation of an intensely blue coloured
L781: ferrous-tripyridyltriazine. Due to the acidic conditions of the FRAP assay it does not include the reducing capacity
L782: of thiols.(15) A standard curve of known concentrations of ferrous ions is used to compare absorbances of Fe [3+]
L783: reacted plasma at 593 nm.
L784: **Nitric oxide (NO) production and metabolism biomarkers**
L785: Nitrite and nitrate concentrations were quantified from EDTA plasma following methanol precipitation of protein
L786: using a dedicated high-performance liquid chromatography system (ENO-20, Amuza Inc. USA).(16) Total
L787: 7
L788: nitrosation products (RXNO) were quantified from EDTA plasma samples using gas-phase chemiluminescence
L789: detection (CLD 77am sp, EcoPhysics, Duernten, Switzerland) of bound NO, following removal of nitrite with
L790: acidified sulfanilamide and reduction of nitroso species by acidic triiodide.(17) Due to the sensitivity of the assay
L791: and the ubiquitous presences of environmental nitrite containing compounds the RXNO assay is particularly
L792: sensitive to contamination during sample processing/storage. RXNO concentrations of >100 nM are
L793: supraphysiological and were deemed extreme outliers and excluded from the final analysis.(17) Cyclic guanosine
L794: monophosphate (cGMP) was measured as a downstream marker of NO signalling. cGMP concentrations were
L795: quantified in EDTA plasma by ELISA (cGMP parameter assay kit R&D Systems).
L796: 8
L797: 4: Expressing the oxygen cost of exercise
L798: During CPET the oxygen cost of performing work (exercise) can be expressed by the slope of the
L799: relationship between the oxygen uptake and work-rate (V̇O2/WR slope). In healthy subjects the
L800: V̇O2/WR (up to maximal exercise intensities) during incremental CPET is surprisingly constant with a
L801: normal range of 10.2 ±1 ml.kg [-1] .W [-1] .(18) A reduced V̇O2/WR is indicative of impaired oxygen delivery
L802: to the muscle. However although a lower V̇O2/WR slope represents less oxygen utilisation per Watt
L803: (suggestive of increased efficiency) it is important to consider in patients with cardiopulmonary
L804: disease, particularly at heavy/vigorous exercise intensities above the anaerobic threshold (AT), this
L805: may represent a developing oxygen debt that is then repaid in recovery.(19) In the present study
L806: recovery data was not available as, due to their lung disease, patients had significant breathlessness
L807: at peak exercise which prevented them being able to tolerate the CPET mask during recovery. In
L808: order to mitigate the impact of a developing oxygen debt during heavy/vigorous exercise intensities
L809: the oxygen cost of exercise was estimated by expressing the V̇O2 work-rate relationship up to the AT.
